mode: "100644"
text: "# Features & Diagnosis\n\nThe TikTok-native growth features, and the diagnostic that routes a stuck account to the skill that\nfixes it. tiktok-growth diagnoses and orchestrates; it doesn't re-do the content.\n\n## Native growth features (use the right one for your stage)\n\n- **Stitch** — clip the start of another video and add your take. Embeds you in an existing\n  conversation; contextual relevance retains viewers and lifts watch time. Great for reactions/hot\n  takes in your niche.\n- **Duet** — pair your video beside a trending/high-visibility one; piggybacks its momentum and\n  exposes you to that creator's audience across FYPs.\n- **Series / Parts (Part 1 / 2 / 3)** — TikTok recommends episode 2 to viewers of episode 1, driving\n  **session depth and follows**. One of the strongest follow-conversion tactics — give people a\n  reason to come back.\n- **Pinned comment** — within the first hour, pin a comment that seeds conversation or points to\n  \"Part 2\" / a resource. Drives comment engagement and watch time.\n- **Video replies to comments** — answer a good comment with a new video; feeds the comment culture\n  and gives you free content ideas that already have demand.\n- **Playlists** — group videos by topic for **bingeing and search** (back-catalog discovery).\n- **LIVE** — algorithmic promotion for active creators + monetization (gifts, subscriptions, live\n  shopping). **Requires ~1,000 followers.** A *community/business* tool for warm fans — **not** an\n  early-growth reach lever.\n\nMatch the feature to the stage: Stitch/Duet/Series help **reach + follows** early; LIVE/playlists\ndeepen an **existing** audience.\n\n## Niche clarity — train the interest graph\n\nTikTok clusters content and viewers by interest (\"sides of TikTok\" — TechTok, BookTok, etc.). A\n**tight, consistent niche** trains the algorithm on who to show you to; a scattered account (gaming +\ncooking + marketing) confuses the interest graph and stalls. Define the lane, reinforce it with\nkeywords (caption/on-screen/audio), and use niche community hashtags to signal which \"side\" you're\non.\n\n## Followers are a business asset, not a reach mechanism\n\nBecause follower count isn't a ranking factor, the goal of growth isn't \"followers for reach.\" It's:\n\n- **Reach** comes from content performance (completion, rewatch, search) — per video.\n- **Followers** are your **owned audience** — they unlock **LIVE** (≥1k), **Shop/affiliate**,\n  repeat-binge of your back-catalog, and a warm base that improves early signals. They're a business\n  outcome, not the reach input.\n\nSo measure reach/views/completion for distribution, and followers/profile-visits/leads for the\nbusiness — don't chase follower count as if it drives reach.\n\n## The diagnosis — symptom → broken stage → fix\n\n| Symptom | Broken stage | Primary fix (skill) |\n|---|---|---|\n| ~200 views then stops | **Phase-1 death** — weak 1-sec hook / low completion | `tiktok-script`, `hook-writer` (hook + completion + loop) |\n| Decent early views, plateaus fast | **Phase-2** — doesn't hold a colder/broader audience | broaden the hook, add a rewatch trigger, less inside-baseball |\n| Views but **few follows** | **Follow-conversion** — no reason to follow / weak profile | `profile-optimization` + **Series** + consistent niche |\n| Not found in search | **Search** — weak keywords | `hashtag-strategy`/`social-seo` + `tiktok-script` keyword layer |\n| One hit, then nothing | **Volume/consistency** — no repeatable system | `content-calendar` + read patterns (`viral-reverse-engineering`) |\n| Scattered, can't get traction | **Niche** — interest graph can't categorize you | tighten the niche/lane |\n| Followers don't engage / no community | **Retention/community** — no relationship | comments, video replies, Series, LIVE (if ≥1k) |\n| Views dropped suddenly in 2026 | **Flux/quality** — algorithm retraining + low-effort detection | fundamentals, original native quality |\n\nMost \"TikTok won't grow\" problems are **one** of these — find which, fix that.\n\n## What doesn't work (skip)\n\n- **Buying followers / engagement / pods** — fake signals hurt performance and risk the account; and\n  followers don't even drive reach.\n- **`#fyp` / generic mega-tags** — no FYP boost; niche/keyword tags only (see `hashtag-strategy`).\n- **Polished, ad-style videos** — underperform vs native; \"make TikToks, not ads.\"\n- **Low-effort volume** — detected and buried; at-bats must be quality-gated.\n- **Quitting after one flop** — single videos are noise; read patterns across many.\n"
